<section id="visa" class="border-t border-hairline">
  <div class="container-px section-pad">
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">
      Visa: the short version
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[60ch] text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Whether you need a visa depends on your passport. Two policies matter for most
      festival travellers.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-field border border-hairline bg-white/60 p-7">
        <p class="font-display text-5xl font-semibold leading-none text-vermilion">76</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-ink">countries, visa-free</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Citizens of 76 countries can enter China visa-free for 30 days, covering most
          of Europe, Japan, South Korea, Australia, New Zealand, and parts of the
          Americas and Middle East.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-field border border-hairline bg-white/60 p-7">
        <p class="font-display text-5xl font-semibold leading-none text-vermilion">55</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold text-ink">countries, 240-hour transit</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          A 10-day transit-free policy at 65 entry ports for 55 countries, ideal for a
          festival stopover on a longer trip through Asia.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      Policies change often. Confirm your passport against the latest National
      Immigration Administration rules before booking.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
